 16 45                                                                                     IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Left  block I   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  The tumor cells do not show overexpression of HER 2 c erbB 2  See note  Note  These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Added by  Grace T  McKee MD Signed On  15 REMOVED_MONTH 03 at 15 05 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left axillary node   is a piece of fibroadipose tissue  measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm  The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a heterogenous yellow and white cut surface  Approximately 17 lymph nodes are located  the largest of which measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 9cm  The nodes are submitted in their entirely in cassettes A C  The largest four lymph nodes are bisected and submitted  half of each are submitted in cassettes D and E  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast lumpectomy   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 3cm lumpectomy specimen  The superior margin is inked blue  the inferior surface is inked black  the lateral surface is inked yellow and the medial surface is inked green  Serial sectioning reveals a well defined white gray  rubbery nodule  grossly abutting the inferior surface  The mass contains some areas of yellow discoloration  The mass measures in its greatest dimension REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 6cm  Representative sections of the mass and its nearest margins are submitted in cassettes F I  Representative sections of breast parenchyma away from the mass are submitted in J and K  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast inferior margin   is an non oriented piece of white yellow fibroadipose tissue  that measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 4cm  The specimen is sectioned and submitted in cassettes L N  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast superior margin   is a non oriented irregular piece of white yellow fibroadipose tissue and measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 4cm  The specimen is serially sectioned and submitted in cassettes O  P  and Q  Resident  JOSHUA B  KISH  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Michele Annette Gadd  M D  PART A  LYMPH NODE  LEFT AXILLA   EXCISION PART B  BREAST LEFT  EXCISIONAL BIOPSY PART C  BREAST LEFT  INFERIOR MARGIN  EXCISON PART D  BREAST LEFT  SUPERIOR MARGIN  EXCISION , Positive.
